<title>UK: Bullough year pretax profit drops 45 pct.</title>
<headline>Bullough year pretax profit drops 45 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to October 31, 1996.</p>
<p>				 (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		3.42		   vs 6.64</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 5.47		   vs 6.05</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 4.30		   vs 4.30</p>
<p> Pretax  profit	   7.99		   vs 14.52</p>
<p> Turnover		   344.67		 vs 343.07</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the British industrial holding company is Bullough Plc. The pretax profit is before exceptional items. The company said profits at its heating division and British office furniture businesses were offset by poor results at Atal, its French office furniture business, and at the refrigeration division. The company, which has sold nine companies since October 1996, said its disposals programme had created a &quot;more focused and profitable group&quot;.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
